Semiconductor Engineering describes a network on chip that moves native, packetized traffic

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:41.560
straight across the boundary between dies.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:46.880
The interface stays fixed so the packet layout is not rewritten where the dies meet.

