Global sources reports Intel's Malaysia team is adding advanced packaging capacity in Penang for AI chips.

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:49.820
New electronics reports IC link from iMac and TSMC are extending their tie-up so more designers

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:56.100
can reach advanced chip design. EE Times reports Indian semiconductor startups are hunting

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:02.380
capital past the seed round. The pinch is the step from prototypes and tape out into volume production.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:08.060
The fiber link is where we take it apart because several colors of light can share one strand

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:10.220
and the cable count does not rise.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:14.060
The ordinary build hands each color a laser of its own,

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.380
then a driver and a control loop.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.540
Color count and parts count climb in lock step.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.680
Every added color is another laser you must feed,

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:25.160
tune and treat as a thing that can fail.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:27.660
A frequency comb breaks that pairing.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:30.020
One source emits many wavelengths,

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:33.140
spaced evenly, and on a spectrum analyzer,

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:34.620
they read like a comb's teeth.

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:40.500
data center knowledge says AI halls are heading for 16 wavelengths on a fiber or

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:45.560
beyond, and that is where a laser for every channel gets heavy. Each new collar

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.780
still drags in a laser, a driver, and a control loop, plus the power, the cost,

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:56.460
and the extra failure points. Solonite chief executive and co-founder Marchello

00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:01.800
Girardi said, four colors is already solved, and that arrays do that job well.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:08.960
He put the start of the hard part at 8. At 16 he said, the pile of components is what limits you.

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:15.860
A single pump laser feeds one silicon nitride die, and that pair emits the full wavelength set at once.

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:20.320
The resonator fixes the grid, and extra channels do not add hardware.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:30.600
Pilot photonics founder and chief technology officer Frank Smith set a comb can crowd far more colors into a tighter span, and interference is not the fear.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:35.880
The gap is born in the resonator, not in a shelf of separate lasers that drift toward

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:36.520
one another.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:40.060
Coems have circulated in telecom research for years.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:45.940
The co-packaged optics these designs picture are still pilot hardware, not a volume line.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:52.200
Four wavelengths is where an array is already enough, and one pump plus pilot co-packaged

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.600
optics is the tougher bet.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:05:00.740
Asuka Fiber for 16 wavelengths and the per-color stack, laser, driver, lock loop, is what

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:05.560
the comb is there to cut, if that one source and the package actually ship in volume.

